CORE smt-backend no-new-smt
main.i
--arch ppc64le --os linux --smt2 --z3
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
On ppc64le, long double is IEEE binary128.  The non-FPA SMT encoding of the
conversion to double used to set bit 20 instead of bit 52 when rounding
overflowed the significand, as it computed 1 << 52 in int.
